      Q('Which ordinance deeply reformed French contract law?', 'the ordinance of 10 February 2016', 'the Villers-Cotterêts ordinance', 'It dates from 1539 and concerns language. 🗣️', 'the 1945 ordinance on minors', 'It concerned juvenile offenders. 👦', 'the Moulins ordinance', 'It dates from the 16th century. 📜', 'It was ratified by a 2018 law.'),
      Q('Which 1985 law improved compensation for road accident victims?', 'the Badinter law', 'the Veil law', 'It concerns abortion. 📜', 'the Kouchner law', 'It concerns patients’ rights. 🏥', 'the Évin law', 'It concerns tobacco and alcohol. 🚭', 'It applies as soon as a land motor vehicle is involved.'),
      Q('What is a penalty clause?', 'a clause setting in advance a sum due in case of non-performance', 'a clause that sends someone to prison', 'Not in civil law! 🔒', 'a forbidden clause', 'It is allowed. ✅', 'a clause about football', 'No. ⚽', 'The judge can reduce it if it is manifestly excessive.'),
      Q('What is the difference between relative and absolute nullity?', 'relative nullity protects a private interest; absolute nullity, the general interest', 'relative nullity is temporary, absolute nullity eternal', 'That is not the criterion. ⏳', 'there is none', 'The rules differ: who can act, time limits… ⚖️', 'relative nullity concerns families', 'No. 👨‍👩‍👧', 'Only the protected person can invoke relative nullity.'),
      Q('What is an offer to contract?', 'a firm and precise proposal to conclude a contract', 'a mere discussion with no commitment', 'That is a negotiation. 💬', 'a present', 'No. 🎁', 'a vague advertisement', 'It is not precise enough. 📢', 'The contract is formed once the acceptance reaches the offeror.'),
      Q('What is unjust enrichment?', 'the duty to compensate the person at whose expense you were enriched without justification', 'getting rich from the lottery', 'That is not unjust! 🍀', 'a salary that is too high', 'No. 💼', 'a year-end bonus', 'No. 🎁', 'It is one of the quasi-contracts, with negotiorum gestio and undue payment.'),
      Q('What is negotiorum gestio (gestion d’affaires)?', 'usefully handling someone else’s affairs without being asked to', 'running a large company', 'Not in the legal sense here. 🏢', 'a business degree', 'No. 🎓', 'managing your own budget', 'No: it is about someone else’s affairs. 💶', 'Example: repairing a leak at an absent neighbour’s home.'),
      Q('What is contractual liability?', 'liability arising from failure to perform a contract', 'liability for harm caused to a stranger', 'That is tort (extra-contractual) liability. 🚶', 'criminal liability', 'It punishes an offence. 🚓', 'parents’ liability', 'That is another kind, vicarious liability. 👨‍👩‍👦', 'The creditor can claim damages.'),
      Q('What is a standard-form contract (contrat d’adhésion)?', 'a contract whose general terms are imposed by one party, without negotiation', 'only a contract to join a club', 'Not only. 🏸', 'a handwritten contract', 'The form does not matter. ✍️', 'a void contract', 'It is valid, but regulated. ✅', 'A clause creating a significant imbalance is deemed unwritten.'),
      Q('Under Article 1240, what does fault-based civil liability require?', 'a fault, damage and a causal link', 'damage alone', 'A fault and a causal link are also needed. 🔗', 'a prior criminal conviction', 'No. 🚓', 'the victim’s agreement', 'No. 🤝', 'It is the former Article 1382 of the Civil Code.')
